  "usageRules": [
    "Global actions, focus indicators, selections, and navigation use Heritage Green; module colors identify content, not button priority.",
    "Use light #F3F6F3 and dark #0D1211 as workspace backgrounds; pure white is not the main light workspace surface.",
    "Prefer neutral surfaces for large tables, forms, and editors; reserve saturated accents for compact chips, icons, and event markers.",
    "Generic Events use Chronicle Copper; specific event types may use their own mapped family.",
    "Sources use Evidence Slate; archive files use Sepia Gold.",
    "Publish-related items use Print Magenta; primary Publish buttons remain Heritage Green.",
    "Never treat a semantic warning or error as interchangeable with similarly colored module accents.",
    "Use a text label or icon as well as color. Provide clear keyboard focus indicators.",
    "Deprecated Leaf Green, Genetic Violet, and Amber Gold tokens are aliases of the three surviving families."
  ],
